During one year, grass in an area stores \(48\,000\text{ kJ}\) of energy as new biomass.

- rabbits eat \(25\%\) of this biomass energy;
- they absorb \(60\%\) of the energy they eat;
- \(20\%\) of the absorbed energy becomes new rabbit biomass;
- foxes eat \(75\%\) of this new rabbit biomass;
- \(10\%\) of the energy eaten by foxes becomes new fox biomass.

How much energy becomes new fox biomass?
